STEP 14 — FINAL WIRING AND RUN

After all files are created:

1. In vite.config.js add a proxy so /api requests in dev go to Django:
   server: { proxy: { '/api': 'http://localhost:8000' } }

2. Update src/api/client.js baseURL to '/api' (so the proxy handles it)

3. Run:
   npm install
   npm run dev

The app should start at http://localhost:5173

Make sure:
- All pages are connected through React Router
- AuthContext wraps the entire app in main.jsx
- Every API call uses the client.js functions (no raw fetch calls anywhere)
- Tailwind classes are used throughout (no separate CSS files except index.css)
- All forms show loading states and error messages
- The booking page works end to end: pick date → pick slot → fill form → confirm

Do not use any paid component libraries. Do not use any external image URLs. All icons should be inline SVG. Build this completely — do not skip any file or section.